             POLYCENTER NETWORKER SAVE AND RESTORE ADDS
         CLIENTSIDE ARCHIVING, WINDOWS NT FOR INTEL SUPPORT


MAYNARD, Mass. -- January 23, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Legato Systems, Inc. today announced new functionality and new 
client support for POLYCENTER NetWorker Save and Restore for DEC 
OSF/1 Alpha, Digital's implementation of Legato Systems' industry-
leading NetWorker product.  Version 3.1 of NetWorker adds clientside 
archiving, a new graphical user interface(GUI), concurrent recovery, 
performance improvements, and new clients, including Windows NT for 
Intel, Windows TCP/IP and a PATHWORKS Windows client.

     According to Gary Gottschalk, Digital's director of storage 
software marketing, "The combination of Legato Systems' technology 
with Digital's StorageWorks architecture and Alpha systems 
performance provides a competitive advantage for Digital's customers 
in reducing operations cost and removing traditional capacity 
barriers.  NetWorker's new archive functionality extends the 
existing NetWorker backup server.  Through a simple point-and-click 
GUI, users can now archive their data, annotate the archive set, 
select archive options and receive automatic notification of archive 
completion."

     Gilbert Wai, senior vice president of product development at 
Legato Systems, said, "These new products provide Digital's 
customers with unique and powerful tools to protect their data and 
to reduce the time for managing their data.  Today's announcement 
continues to establish Legato as a visionary in the storage 
management marketplace."

     POLYCENTER NetWorker Save and Restore software provides the 
industry leading Legato Networker technology ported to DEC OSF/1 
Alpha platforms.  The software supports a wide variety of client 
platforms and the most popular storage media, including digital 
linear tape(DLT) devices.  Digital is bundling the single system 
version of NetWorker Save and Restore with all its OSF/1 systems and 
has included the NetWorker backup server in the DEC OSF/1 NAS server 
packages sold with most AlphaServer systems.  These two promotions 
make it easy to upgrade to full NetWorker capabilities through the 
addition of client, jukebox and archive licenses.  

     Legato Systems, Inc., headquartered in Palo Alto, Calif., is 
the leader in scalable network data storage management software 
products that simplify administration for networked computers.  
Legato NetWorker is the first client/server network storage 
management application that is independent of hardware platforms, 
operating systems and backup devices.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
