                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION
                             FACT SHEET



PRODUCT NAME: POLYCENTER NetWorker Save and Restore V3.1 for DEC OSF/1 ALPHA
             

HIGHLIGHTS:

Several new enhancements make NetWorker an even more powerful tool 
to automate your multivendor backup operational needs.  

Our new release of NetWorker:


   o  Extends your backup operations to include archive

   o  Includes your Windows@tm NT Intel clients now

   o  Available for shipment in March


PRODUCT DESCRIPTION:

POLYCENTER NetWorker Save and Restore V3.1 software for DEC OSF/1 
Alpha systems provides online, automated backup for multivendor 
systems in networked TCP/IP environments.  NetWorker V3.1 adds many 
new functions including clientside archiving, a new graphical user 
interface for easier use, concurrent recovery for more efficiency, 
performance improvements, recover by savesets, barcode label 
support, data set clones, and new clients including Windows NT 
for Intel, Windows TCP/IP and a PATHWORKS Windows client.

NetWorker archive functionality leverages the user's existing 
investment in, and the strength of, the NetWorker backup and 
recovery product.  The NetWorker archive server option allows file 
archiving and retrieval services and is an extension to the existing 
NetWorker backup server.  Through a simple point and click 
interface, users can archive their data, annotate the archive set, 
select archive options and receive automatic notification of archive 
completion.

Windows NT client support is available for Intel clients now.  
Additionally, NT Alpha will be available later this year.


CUSTOMER BENEFITS:

Backup operations are critical and can be cumbersome.  With 
NetWorker, your back up operations are easy to complete, quickly 
and reliably.  NetWorker V3.1 ensures consistent, reliable data 
protection for the entire network.  Most customers want one 
automated tool to solve their backup needs.  NetWorker continues 
to meet these needs and more.  

NetWorker V3.1 provides

   -  conservation of online storage while protecting critical 
      corporate data with our new archiving functionality

   -  more client platform support with Windows NT Intel and Windows 
      TCP/IP support

   -  improved data protection with save set cloning, which allows 
      you to make multiple copies of the backup data.

   -  broadened storage device support to meet growing needs--
      including DLT and StorageWorks Tape Library TL820

   -  quicker and easier data recovery with parallel recovery which 
      allows multiple recoveries to be performed in parallel from 
      the same media.

   -  more automation with support for bar code labeling

   -  faster, better and easier to use graphical user interface. 
      NetWorker now has a distinct and separate interface for end 
      users and system administrators


COMPETITIVE ANALYSIS:

POLYCENTER NetWorker Save and Restore software provides the industry
leading Legato NetWorker@tm technology ported to DEC OSF/1 Alpha 
platforms.  This technology was chosen by "Network Computing" as one 
of the "10 network products you can't live without." (April 1994)

The combination of Alpha hardware performance, StorageWorks support, 
and NetWorker software for DEC OSF/1 ALPHA platforms provides a 
distinct competitive advantage. The software supports a wide variety 
of client platforms with a DEC OSF/1 server.  In addition, the most 
popular media is supported including digital linear tape (DLT) 
devices.


CHANNELS:

NetWorker V3.1 is sold through DECdirect, Digital's business 
partners and our local Digital sales offices.


AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING:

NetWorker Save and Restore V3.1 software will be available in March.  
The NT Intel client will be available in late January.  Client kits 
will be updated to include archive software and documentation and 
will be available in March.

To add archiving functionality to an existing NetWorker environment, 
upgrade the NetWorker backup license to V3.1 functionality.  Also, 
add the NetWorker Archive Server addon license and client licenses 
for each archive client.  You will also need to upgrade the NSR 
client kits to obtain the archive client software and documentation.
                          
Each client connection is licensed.  For example, if there are 10 
backup clients and each will also archive data, then 20 client 
licenses are required. 
 
Server prices range from $2500 to $5500.  Client licenses range from 
$75 for PC/NT to $160 for UNIX.  Documentation is approximately $120 
and is recommended.   
