            DIGITAL ANNOUNCES RECORD-BREAKING PERFORMANCE
                        AND PRICE/PERFORMANCE


    Alpha Servers with Windows NT are the Fastest Servers Running
                        Microsoft SQL Server


MAYNARD, Mass. -- January 24, 1995 -- New AlphaServer systems and 
Microsoft SQL Server for the Microsoft Windows NT Server network 
operating system have set performance and price/performance records 
in independently audited tests defined by the Transaction Processing 
Performance Council (TPC). 

     The results, announced today by Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Microsoft Corporation, are as follows: performance of 174.2 tpsB 
at $413/tpsB for a one-processor AlphaServer 1000 4/200 and 308.8 
tpsB at $423/tpsB for a two-processor AlphaServer 2100 4/275. No 
other computer vendor has released TPC-B performance and 
price/performance figures for the Windows NT network operating 
system that compare to these. These results were achieved with the 
Windows NT Version 3.5 network operating system and Microsoft SQL 
Server relational database management system. 

     "These results unquestionably show the powerful combination of 
Digital's AlphaServer systems and the Microsoft BackOffice family of 
products, which includes Microsoft SQL Server," said Jim Allchin, 
senior vice president of the Business Systems Division at Microsoft. 
"Digital's servers and Microsoft's software offer customers real 
business value through powerful and scalable solutions for 
mission-critical applications."

     Digital and Microsoft will continue to provide systems with 
leadership performance and price/performance, according to Pauline 
Nist, vice president of Digital's Alpha Server Business Segment. "At 
$413/tpsB, the AlphaServer 1000 system provides customers with the 
best value of any system running Windows NT Server software. And in 
the future, Microsoft SQL Server customers can look forward to even 
greater performance with the AlphaServer 2100 -- the fastest Windows 
NT Server on the market -- through cost-effective upgrades." 

Digital's Servers for Windows NT are Most Cost-Effective

     Customers everywhere are moving to client/server solutions for 
new business-critical applications, and they're saying that price/
performance is one of the most important factors in choosing a 
solution. 

     Reuben H. Donnelley Corporation is the world's oldest publisher 
of Yellow Page phone books.  The corporation is now pioneering the 
use of distributed voice processing for a new product -- the 
Interactive Yellow Pages -- where users can access all kinds of 
information from a computerized database using just a telephone and 
the Yellow Pages. "We're implementing a client/server environment, 
and the cost effectiveness will come from using standardized 
products that offer more performance at much lower costs. 
AlphaServer systems running Windows NT and Microsoft SQL Server 
software have greatly expanded what we can do," said systems and 
development manager Stephen Jamison.

     The Best Buy Company, Inc. is the nation's fastest growing 
retailer of consumer electronics. The company has just introduced 
interactive multimedia kiosks as a way for consumers to learn about 
products, from a complete run-down on features to prices. "We were 
looking for a processor that could take high-quality video and serve 
up to 12 kiosks simultaneously throughout our stores.  We found that 
Digital's AlphaServer 2100 systems running Microsoft SQL Server give 
us great price/performance, and enable us to bring multimedia 
information to our customers cost effectively," said Steve Anderson, 
CIO and senior vice president of MIS at the Best Buy Company.

     Microsoft's BackOffice family of products includes Windows NT 
Server, Microsoft SQL Server, Systems Management Server, SNA Server, 
and Microsoft Mail. It is an integrated suite of client/server 
applications designed to work together, making it easier for 
companies to improve decision making and streamline business 
processes.

     Digital's AlphaServer 1000 4/200 is a low-cost, highly 
dependable, deskside server, featuring one 200 MHz processor. The 
AlphaServer 2100 4/275 is a more expandable model that can 
incorporate up to four 275 MHz processors, and features large memory 
and storage capacity. Both servers are available in high-capacity, 
space-saving rackmount configurations. Digital's AlphaServers offer 
balanced system performance through high-performance processors and 
high throughput I/O. They are also highly reliable, upgradeable 
through cost-effective in-cabinet processor upgrades, and use 
standard components and peripherals.

Microsoft and Digital Partnership Delivers Solutions

     Digital and Microsoft are working together to deliver mission-
critical enterprise solutions to customers.  This includes joint 
marketing programs and campaigns, customer support, consulting, and 
training. The partnership provides experience implementing, 
integrating, and supporting business solutions for customers. 
Digital is a worldwide Microsoft Authorized Support Center, with 
locations throughout the world. Digital is also Microsoft's largest 
training partner in the world. 

     The TPC-B benchmark was designed as an appropriate yardstick 
for servers in a database environment. The TPC-B benchmark is a 
back-end database test that exercises the database components 
necessary to support update-intensive database services.  This 
environment is characterized by significant disk input/output, 
moderate system and application execution time, and transaction 
integrity. 

     Founded in 1975, Microsoft (NASDAQ "MSFT"), is the world leader 
in software for personal computers. The company offers a wide range 
of products and services for business and personal use, each 
designed with the mission of making it easier and more enjoyable for 
people to take advantage of the full power of personal computing 
every day.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
